:279097162,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTcxNjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/discussion","name":"discussion","color":"ccaaff","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-08-06T14:31:11Z","updated_at":"2026-08-21T18:03:32Z","closed_at":"2026-08-21T18:01:08Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122168","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122168","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122168.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122168.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #121927\r\n\r\n`PrimitiveMesh.flip_faces` did not work correctly for meshes without an index array.\r\n\r\nThis change makes `flip_faces` work for non-indexed meshes by swapping the vertex order when no indices are available. It also allows face flipping when normals are missing by handling normals and indices independently.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nI used AI assistance to help understand the issue and review the changes.\r\n\r\nPreviously, `flip_faces` only applied when both normals and indices existed. As a result, non-indexed meshes ignored the setting completely.\r\n\r\nThis keeps the existing behavior for indexed meshes while adding support for non-indexed meshes.","closed_by":{"login":"globuskk","id":312095415,"node_id":"U_kgDOEpoytw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312095415?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api